        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: enable array fill lint rule",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOxlint 1.72 added `unicorn/no-array-fill-with-reference-type`, which catches arrays whose elements accidentally share one mutable object. OpenClaw currently inherits the rule through the broad `suspicious` category, but the curated rule list does not record that policy explicitly.\n\nFollow-up to #100027 and #100083.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Pins `unicorn/no-array-fill-with-reference-type` at error severity.\n- Preserves the existing effective lint behavior while making the intended guard durable and reviewable.\n- Avoids enabling the noisy style-only rules introduced in the same Oxlint release.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior change. Future attempts to initialize an array with one shared mutable reference fail lint explicitly.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox-through-Crabbox: `tbx_01kwqt12gtgnft4w8wxepgt8dx`.\n- `pnpm check:changed`: passed.\n- Full `pnpm lint`: core 0 warnings/errors; plugins 0 warnings/errors; scripts 0 warnings/errors.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: clean, 0.99 confidence.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n",
